
## Bandit Level 16 → Level 17

**Challenge:** 

The credentials for the next level can be retrieved by submitting the password of the current level to a port on localhost in the range 31000 to 32000. 
First find out which of these ports have a server listening on them. Then find out which of those speak SSL/TLS and which don’t. There is only 1 server 
that will give the next credentials, the others will simply send back to you whatever you send to it.

Helpful note: Getting “DONE”, “RENEGOTIATING” or “KEYUPDATE”? Read the “CONNECTED COMMANDS” section in the manpage.

Commands you may need to solve this level
ssh, telnet, nc, ncat, socat, openssl, s_client, nmap, netstat, ss


**Solution & Explanation:****
```
STEP 1: cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit16
# read the current password (bandit16)
# this is what we’ll submit to the correct service

STEP 2: nmap -p 31000-32000 localhost
# scans localhost ports 31000 through 32000
# shows which ports are open (services actually listening)

STEP 3: openssl s_client -connect localhost:PORT -ign_eof
# test each open port from the scan results
# we are looking for the one that responds like an SSL service that expects a password

STEP 4: Enter bandit16 password
# send the bandit16 password into that SSL connection
# the correct port will respond with an SSH private key (starts with “-----BEGIN ... PRIVATE KEY-----”)

STEP 5: exit, vim L17key.private
# exit from overthewire server back into local host and add contents from the SSH private key to a vim file named L17key.private within local host

STEP 6: chmod 600 bandit17.key
# lock down key permissions so SSH will accept it

STEP 7: ssh -i L17key.private bandit17@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220
# ssh → connect to another account
# -i L17key.private → use this private key to authenticate
# bandit17@bandit.labs.overthewire.org → log in as user bandit17 and connect to the remote machine called bandit.labs.overthewire.org
# -p 2220 → Bandit SSH runs on port 2220

STEP 8: cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit17
# now that you're logged in as bandit17, you have permission to read it
# the output is the password for bandit17



```
